# Accepted infrastructure risks for this low-cost student lab (trivy config on terraform/).
# Every entry is explained in the README ("Terraform infrastructure"); everything else must pass.

# AWS-0040: the EKS API keeps a public endpoint so kubectl can run from a laptop without a VPN or
# bastion. It only accepts var.api_allowed_cidrs (your own IP); nodes use the private endpoint.
AWS-0040

# AWS-0164: the subnets give nodes public IPs because the lab has no NAT gateway (billed every hour).
# The EKS cluster security group only accepts traffic from the cluster itself.
# Production: private subnets for nodes behind a NAT gateway.
AWS-0164
